.TH SYSTEMD-SENTRY.CONF 5 "September 2026" "systemd-sentry 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
systemd-sentry.conf, policy.toml \- configuration and policy format for systemd-sentry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/config.toml
.br
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/policy.toml
.br
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/policy.d/*.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-sentry
reads its primary operational configuration from
\fI/etc/systemd-sentry/config.toml\fR and its safety and remediation policy from
\fI/etc/systemd-sentry/policy.toml\fR.
.PP
Following systemd conventions, drop-in policy extensions may be placed in
\fI/etc/systemd-sentry/policy.d/*.toml\fR. Drop-ins are parsed in lexicographical
sort order; individual unit policy declarations override global defaults.
.SH CONFIG.TOML SECTIONS
.TP
.B [daemon]
General daemon operational parameters:
.RS
.TP
.BI socket_path= "PATH"
Path to the UNIX domain IPC socket (default: \fI/run/systemd-sentry/sentry.sock\fR).
.TP
.BI watchdog_sec= "SECONDS"
Watchdog notification interval (default: 15).
.TP
.BI max_rss_bytes= "BYTES"
Resident Set Size memory limit before load shedding (default: 13631488, 13 MiB).
.RE
.TP
.B [provider]
AI diagnostic provider configuration:
.RS
.TP
.BI provider_type= "TYPE"
Diagnostic engine: \fI"llamacpp"\fR, \fI"openai"\fR, or \fI"fallback"\fR.
.TP
.BI endpoint= "URL"
HTTP endpoint for the inference provider.
.TP
.BI model= "NAME"
Model name (e.g. \fI"llama3:8b"\fR or \fI"gpt-4o-mini"\fR).
.TP
.BI api_key= "KEY"
Authentication token. When running under systemd with credentials, the key is
automatically read from \fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/openai_api_key\fR or
\fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/api_key\fR without plaintext storage on disk.
.RE
.SH POLICY.TOML SECTIONS
.TP
.B [global]
Defines baseline safety rules across all supervised units:
.RS
.TP
.B protected_units
List of unit names that the supervisor is strictly forbidden from restarting or
mutating. Default protected units include:
.IR systemd-journald.service ,
.IR systemd-logind.service ,
.IR systemd-udevd.service ,
.IR systemd-resolved.service ,
.IR dbus.service ,
.IR sshd.service ,
.IR ssh.service ,
.IR init.scope ,
and
.IR systemd-sentry.service .
.TP
.B allowed_actions
Set of permissible remediation actions: \fI"RestartWithBackoff"\fR, \fI"Reload"\fR,
\fI"ResetFailed"\fR, or \fI"NotifyOnly"\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B [circuit]
Sliding-window circuit breaker tuning:
.RS
.TP
.BI max_failures= "N"
Maximum failures tolerated in the sliding window before tripping (default: 3).
.TP
.BI window_secs= "SECONDS"
Duration of the failure evaluation sliding window (default: 60).
.TP
.BI cooldown_secs= "SECONDS"
Base cooldown duration before transitioning to half-open state (default: 30).
Trips back off exponentially up to \fImax_cooldown_secs\fR (default: 1800).
.TP
.BI flap_threshold= "N"
Number of circuit trips within the flap window before locking out permanently (default: 3).
.TP
.BI flap_window_secs= "SECONDS"
Window duration for flap detection (default: 900).
.RE
.TP
.BI [units. UNIT_NAME ]
Per-unit configuration overrides:
.RS
.TP
.BI allowed_actions= "[...]"
Explicitly permitted actions for this specific unit.
.TP
.BI max_failures= "N"
Unit-specific failure threshold.
.TP
.BI auto_remediate= "BOOLEAN"
Enable or disable automated remediation for this service.
.RE
.SH SECURITY
File sizes for policy configurations are strictly bounded to at most 64 KiB to
prevent denial-of-service or memory bloat. Malformed drop-in files are safely
logged and skipped without crashing the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-sentry (1),
.BR systemd-sentry.service (8),
.BR systemd-creds (1)
